  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training for Cosmetics Regulators in Developing Countires in Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen safety and quality management levels and regulatory capabilities for cosmetics regulators in developing countries in Asia, contribute to improving the quality of life of the people in the recipient country, and share know-how in improving the domestic cosmetics regulatory system to enhance the image of a leading regulatory country.    In additions, it seeks to harmonize cosmetics regulations through information exchange and cooperation with cosmetics regulators of ASEAN countries, thereby eliminating non-tariff trade barriers, and contributing to the expansion of cosmetics export markets and diversification of exporting countries by allowing the domestic cosmetics industry to enter the markets of developing Asian countries. Therefore, this project aims to share the excellence of Koreas cosmetics safety management system, strengthen the capacity of beneficiary countries cosmetics safety management policies, and lead global cosmetics regulations.   The ultimate goal is to introduce Koreas cosmetics safety management policy and system by year, educate on excellent domestic systems, and share insights on cosmetics safety management with developing countries in Asia through on-site visits to CGMP manufacturing facilities, and establish a plan to improve regulations in the Asian region based on the domestic regulatory system.</narrative>
  </description>
